Using a)pply for polearms is already its own problem, but with nothing
similar already in existence it was one of the better ways to handle it.
It is, however, definitely not intuitive and is a common question in
#nethack from new players on NAO: "how do i use the polearm?"  Adding
more unintuitive behavior to a)pply doesn't improve the situation.

People already have trouble distinguishing between 't'hrow and 'f'ire; I
am not going to increase that confusion by creating a third command to
handle ranged combat.  Right now if people don't use the % "pick
launcher" command, they'll be no worse off than before; if they do, they
will be able to use the same command they always have to shoot missiles
and will get the benefits of the improvement.

